Description: Offer the xdg-session-management-v1 Wayland protocol.
 Backport of mutter merge request 4806 to 50.1. Mutter 50 has the session management protocol only under its
 draft name xx_session_manager_v1, and offers it only when gnome-shell runs with
 MUTTER_DEBUG_SESSION_MANAGEMENT_PROTOCOL=1. Clients which implement the final protocol, like Firefox since 154,
 bind only xdg_session_manager_v1, so they never find it. With this patch mutter offers xdg_session_manager_v1
 to every client, and a client which names its windows has their workspace, monitor, position, size and
 maximized, tiled or fullscreen state restored by mutter the next time it opens a window with that name.
 .
 The four commits are cherry-picked unchanged except for the test change of the last one. Upstream it edits
 src/tests/wayland-xdg-session-management-tests.c, which was split out of src/tests/wayland-unit-tests.c after
 50.1, so here the same line is removed from wayland-unit-tests.c instead. The protocol XML is mutter's own copy,
 which src/meson.build uses when wayland-protocols is older than 1.48, as it is in Ubuntu 26.04.
Author: Carlos Garnacho <carlosg@gnome.org>
Origin: backport, https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter/-/merge_requests/4806
Applied-Upstream: 51.beta, commits e14fc49862d0c1f7b8f66be42a7912bf5cdda71c 8366f508916e4e71426400b499568c2e4d01af86
 10043bf53367092e1b753dfb0c4325a508628c73 81875dabd439fe2be19ccce82407575b9ee188e9
Last-Update: 2026-11-02
